<h2>Games</h2>
I've created several interactive games that run right in your browser using Blazor WebAssembly:
<br><br>
<strong>Word Games:</strong><br>
Try the Blazor version of my word games right on this web site. They are Blazor Web assembly in C# running entirely in the browser. I wrote them with GitHub Copilot by pointing it to <a href="https://github.com/calvinhsia/WordScape">my Xamarin game code</a>.
<br>
<a href="wordscape">🎯 WordScape</a> - Drag letters around the circle to fill in the grid with words
<br>
<a href="wordament">🎲 Wordament</a> - Find words in a 4x4 grid by connecting adjacent letters
<br><br>
<strong>Programming & Graphics:</strong><br>
<a href="logo">🐢 Logo Turtle Graphics</a> - Learn programming by commanding a turtle to draw amazing pictures! Based on the classic Logo programming language inspired by Cynthia Solomon in 1967, you can create geometric patterns, spirals, flowers and more using simple commands like "fd 100" (forward 100 steps) and "rt 90" (right turn 90 degrees).
<br>
<a href="cartoon">🎬 Cartoon Animation</a> - Create frame-by-frame animations by drawing on a canvas. Draw, save frames, and watch your cartoon come to life! Demonstrated at Honolulu Academy of Arts in 1984
<br><br>
<strong>Simulations & Physics:</strong><br>
<a href="bounce">⚽ Bounce Physics</a> - Watch bouncing balls with realistic physics! Adjust gravity, elasticity, and add more balls by clicking. Based on classic physics simulations.
<br>
<a href="fish">🐠 Fish Aquarium</a> - Watch fish and sharks swim around in a predator prey simulation with realistic movement and behaviors.
<br>
<img src="images/WordGames.png" alt="WordGame picture" style="width:200px;height:300px;">
<br>
The word games use English dictionaries at <a href="https://www.nuget.org/packages/DictionaryLib_Calvin_Hsia/">https://www.nuget.org/packages/DictionaryLib_Calvin_Hsia/</a>
<br>
<a href="https://github.com/calvinhsia/WordScape">Word Games Source code</a>
